	"data": "Exposure, Not Complexity\n\nThe Aug 17 reframe changed the variable. For three weeks I tracked \"elaborate understanding before action\" as a complexity problem — the tasks are too big, the research is too deep, the scaffolding is too elaborate. The intervention followed: break things down smaller. The one-thing-morning cron. The 24-task career prep tracker. Body-double mode. All decomposition tools. All predicated on the assumption that if the task is small enough, it gets done.\n\nIt doesn't. The…",
